`references/commands-quick-ref.md` is verbatim from that commit.

Edits in `SKILL.md`:
- Shortened the description and set `disable-model-invocation: true`, with
  OpenCode auto-invoke off. The description names zanven-pc (RTX 4070).
- Capture and replay run only on zanven-pc. Cloud VMs and the bot box hand
  those steps off. The upstream MCP server is not included.
- Install line is `pip install rdc-cli==0.7.0`.
- Removed the lux-playground / `D:\` capture helper. Example paths are
  relative (`captures/`). Windows-only module names (`renderdoc.pyd`,
  `renderdoc.dll`, `renderdoccmd.exe`) and the HKCU Vulkan implicit-layer
  registry key are marked Windows-only. Linux uses `renderdoc.so` and
  `VK_ADD_LAYER_PATH` or `implicit_layer.d`.

Edits in `references/debugging-recipes.md`:
- Added a banner: capture and replay run only on zanven-pc (RTX 4070).
- Replaced `D:/renderdoc/captures/` with `captures/`.
- Replaced `cd D:/shaderlang &&` with `cd /path/to/app &&`.

The skill files at that commit are byte-identical to the later copy in
https://github.com/Ugbot/ai-grind at plugin/skills/renderdoc-gpu-debug/
(commit 4d6c3643ae5e1c591fcebbeda9fc931ca21bf818). This pin is the original
skill commit. Upstream master de33576fa0a4ee739b4b0434d10d710880d604c6 only
adds the MCP server, which is not included.

